# Provisional Application

This scope computes the earliest date on which a provisionally
applied agreement can be terminated, given a required advance
notice period.

Source pattern: exchange-of-letters agreements applied de facto
before formal entry into force, common in EU textile and trade
agreements.
Example: "the European Community is prepared to apply de facto,
from 1 January 1995, the modifications [...] on the
understanding that either Party may at any time terminate this
de facto application of the amended Agreement provided that one
hundred and twenty days notice is given."

```catala
declaration scope ProvisionalApplication:
  input provisional_start content date
  input termination_notice content duration
  output earliest_termination content date
```

## Earliest termination

The earliest date on which the agreement can be terminated is
the provisional start date plus the required notice period.

```catala
scope ProvisionalApplication:
  date round down
  definition earliest_termination equals
    provisional_start + termination_notice
```
